Package: ubuntuguard-agent
Version: @DEB_VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Depends: @DEB_DEPENDS@
Maintainer: @DEB_MAINTAINER@
Homepage: @DEB_HOMEPAGE@
Installed-Size: @DEB_INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: UbuntuGuard endpoint agent with USB device control
 The UbuntuGuard agent reports this laptop's inventory to the UbuntuGuard
 server and applies the USB device policy an administrator sets in the
 dashboard. It installs two systemd services: an unprivileged agent that
 talks to the network, and a root enforcer that changes usbguard rules. The
 two communicate over a local Unix socket, so the component exposed to the
 network is not the component holding privilege.
 .
 Installing this package does NOT enrol the laptop. Enrollment consumes a
 single-use token and creates an auditable device identity, so it is a
 deliberate action with a person behind it rather than a side effect of
 unpacking a package. After installing, open "Enrol this laptop with
 UbuntuGuard" from the applications menu and paste the token your
 administrator sent you.
 .
 This package carries no credential of any kind. The device's private key is
 generated on this laptop during enrollment and never leaves it.
